  "currentRoundInspection": {
    "inspectedOn": "2026-10-15",
    "scope": "Four actually inspected exterior pictures:undated full front,2006 and2012 eastern choir exteriors,and distant hazy2026 aerial used for broad silhouette only.No bespoke plans/surveys researched or photographs redistributed.Hidden/current nave detail and exact height datum remain approximate.",
    "pictures": [
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Katedra_Poznan_front.jpg",
        "author": "Not credited in the Commons file metadata",
        "date": null,
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-3.0 migrated / GFDL",
        "observed": "Actually inspected complete western front. Twin tall square red-brick towers with narrow lower openings carry dark green copper belfry stages and tiered Baroque caps/crosses. A clock is visible on the southern front tower. Between them,a large recessed pointed portal/window field rises beneath a stepped Gothic gable with slender pale recessed vertical panels and brick piers. Several smaller copper-capped eastern towers appear behind. Trees obscure some lower front,original capture date unspecified;fine doorway/sculptural detail remains approximate."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Katedra_od_po%C5%82udnia_Pozna%C5%84_RB1.JPG",
        "author": "Radomil",
        "date": "2006-09-24",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-3.0 migrated / GFDL",
        "observed": "Actually inspected eastern choir view;file name suggests south but visible geometry is the eastern side as its own description states. Three smaller red-brick faceted towers with Gothic lancets carry swelling copper roofs,actual open narrow lanterns and upper onions/crosses around a steep green choir roof. Low pale-plaster ambulatory/chapels have round-headed windows and green roofs;the projecting eastern chapel has a shallow copper dome and pilasters/simplified corner figures. Twin taller western towers are visible behind. Fine carving/statues and exact hidden nave bays remain approximate."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Katedra_p.w._%C5%9B%C5%9B._Piotra_i_Paw%C5%82a_w_Poznaniu.jpg",
        "author": "Mkos",
        "date": "2012-11-11",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-3.0-PL",
        "observed": "Actually inspected clearer full eastern choir exterior. Three smaller faceted brick towers have tall pointed glazing and pale eave bands,bulbous oxidized-copper caps,open lantern columns and narrow upper onion profiles. A dominant pitched green choir roof connects them. Lower cream/pale-yellow plaster ambulatory contains repeated round-headed windows and a projecting domed chapel with pilasters,cornices and simplified figures. Front pair have dark copper belfries/louver fields above red-brick shafts. Hidden side rhythms,current finishes and precise sculpture remain estimates."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Katedra_Pozna%C5%84ska_w_porannej_mgle_z_lotu_ptaka,_02.03.2026,_Lesiex.jpg",
        "author": "Lesiex",
        "date": "2026-03-02",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Actually inspected distant aerial city photograph. Supports overall twin tall western towers,lower long cathedral and green rear caps only. Cathedral occupies a small hazy part of the picture;not used for detailed roof/window controls."
      }
    ]
